{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A table needs three things: a column definition, a data source that answers","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"how many rows there are and what each cell’s value is, and a place in a view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hierarchy. Everything else is optional.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Add the package","type":"heading","anchor":"Add-the-package"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Gingham is a Swift package for macOS 14 on Apple silicon and iOS and iPadOS 17 and later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Intel Macs aren’t supported).","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In Xcode:"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" choose File > Add Package Dependencies, click Add Local to pick","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the package folder (or enter its Git URL), and add the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gingham","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" library to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"your app target.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Package.swift"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"strong"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"code":["dependencies: [","    .package(url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/digitalglobeby\/Gingham\", from: \"1.8.0\"),  \/\/ or .package(path: \"..\/Gingham\")","],","targets: [","    .target(name: \"MyApp\", dependencies: [\"Gingham\"]),","]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Then ","type":"text"},{"code":"import Gingham","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" where you use it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A minor version may add cases to the enums that describe values, formats,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"filters and summaries (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHValueFormat","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHColumnFilter","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHCellValue","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHAggregate","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and the like): keep a ","type":"text"},{"code":"default","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over them, and updates won’t stop your code from compiling.","type":"text"}]},{"name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Linked as the binary "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Gingham.xcframework"},{"type":"text","text":", Gingham’s enums may get"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"new cases in later versions, so a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over one needs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@unknown default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(an error in Swift 6 without it). "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHColumnItem","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHDataColumnItem","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHColumnPin","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHColumnVisibility\/State","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are frozen: their cases are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all there will be. "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHCellValue","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHNamedColor","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" are frozen too, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an app makes values as fast as Gingham does, but a minor version may still"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"add cases to them: keep a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"default"},{"type":"text","text":" in a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" over them."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","type":"aside"},{"level":3,"text":"Define the columns","type":"heading","anchor":"Define-the-columns"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Columns are values of ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableColumn","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", listed as ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHColumnItem","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":"s. Each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column has an ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which is also the key the data source answers values for:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["let columns: [GHColumnItem] = [","    .column(GHTableColumn(\"name\", title: \"Campaign\", width: 220, pin: .leading)),","    .column(GHTableColumn(\"status\", title: \"Status\", width: 120)),","    .column(GHTableColumn(\"spend\", title: \"Spend\", width: 120,","                          alignment: .automatic, format: .currency(code: \"EUR\"),","                          summary: .aggregate(.sum))),","    .column(GHTableColumn(\"clicks\", title: \"Clicks\", width: 100,","                          alignment: .automatic, format: .number(fractionDigits: 0),","                          summary: .aggregate(.sum))),","]"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"pin: .leading","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" freezes the name column at the leading edge; ","type":"text"},{"code":"alignment: .automatic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" aligns numbers to the trailing edge. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/DefiningColumns","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Provide the data","type":"heading","anchor":"Provide-the-data"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The data source is any class that adopts ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableViewDataSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Keep your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"records in an array and answer from it:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["struct Campaign {","    var id: String","    var name: String","    var status: String","    var spend: Double","    var clicks: Int","}","","@MainActor","final class CampaignTableData: GHTableViewDataSource {","    var campaigns: [Campaign] = []","","    func numberOfRows(in tableView: GHTableView) -> Int {","        campaigns.count","    }","","    func tableView(_ tableView: GHTableView, valueFor column: GHTableColumn, row: Int) -> GHCellValue {","        let campaign = campaigns[row]","        switch column.id {","        case \"id\": return .text(campaign.id)","        case \"name\": return .text(campaign.name)","        case \"status\": return .text(campaign.status)","        case \"spend\": return .number(campaign.spend)","        case \"clicks\": return .number(Double(campaign.clicks))","        default: return .empty","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Return ","type":"text"},{"code":".empty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for columns you don’t know: the table may ask about columns","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"that aren’t shown, such as the inputs of a summary formula.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Show the table","type":"heading","anchor":"Show-the-table"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that scrolls by itself. Add it directly to your","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view (not inside an ","type":"text"},{"code":"NSScrollView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and pin it with Auto Layout:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["final class CampaignsViewController: NSViewController, GHTableViewDelegate {","    private let data = CampaignTableData()","    private let table = GHTableView(frame: .zero)","","    override func loadView() {","        let root = NSView()","        table.columns = columns","        table.rowIdentifierColumnID = \"id\"          \/\/ Keeps the selection on the same campaigns.","        table.autosaveName = \"CampaignsTable\"       \/\/ Remembers the user's columns.","        table.emptyStateText = \"No campaigns\"","        table.dataSource = data","        table.delegate = self","        table.translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = false","        root.addSubview(table)","        NSLayoutConstraint.activate([","            table.topAnchor.constraint(equalTo: root.topAnchor),","            table.leadingAnchor.constraint(equalTo: root.leadingAnchor),","            table.trailingAnchor.constraint(equalTo: root.trailingAnchor),","            table.bottomAnchor.constraint(equalTo: root.bottomAnchor),","        ])","        view = root","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The table holds its data source and delegate weakly: keep them alive, as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"view controller above does with ","type":"text"},{"code":"data","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Update the data","type":"heading","anchor":"Update-the-data"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Whenever the records change, change them and call","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/reloadData()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" right away:","type":"text"}]},{"code":["func show(_ campaigns: [Campaign]) {","    data.campaigns = campaigns","    table.reloadData()","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"name":"Important","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reloadData()"},{"type":"text","text":" immediately after replacing the data, before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"selecting rows, scrolling or returning to the run loop. Until then the table"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"still asks about the old rows, which may no longer exist, and an index out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of range would crash your data source."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","type":"aside"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Setting ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/ngtable.Gingham\/documentation\/Gingham\/GHTableView\/dataSource","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" also reloads the table.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Try the demo","type":"heading","anchor":"Try-the-demo"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The package contains a demo app with ad campaign data. Open the package in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Xcode, choose the ","type":"text"},{"code":